{
  "_comment": [
    "US-124 / ADR 0091 corpus oracle, re-pinned 2026-09-08 for US-127 / ADR 0102",
    "from the app's own parser (window.__braAutoModeDebug.dxf.parse on",
    "dxf.decodeBytes(<file bytes>)). 'patterns' = pieces the parser must return;",
    "for every INSERT-based file it equals the top-level INSERT count now that",
    "duplicate block names resolve k-th INSERT -> k-th BLOCK and GBK names decode",
    "correctly. 'orphans' must be 0 everywhere.",
    "'lines' = kept segments; 'droppedExact' / 'droppedQv' / 'degenerate' pin what",
    "the three drop paths removed (exact duplicates, ASTM quality-validation twins,",
    "and - new in US-127 - geometry of length zero, which the native measurement",
    "parser had always rejected while the board parser kept it and drew it as a dot).",
    "",
    "What US-127 / ADR 0102 changed, and why the rows below moved:",
    "  1. Zero-length LINEs and repeated polyline vertices are rejected by BOTH",
    "     parsers now, so 'lines' drops by the file's 'degenerate' count and the",
    "     hops that used to be counted as 'droppedExact' are counted as",
    "     'degenerate' instead. 838 such segments were being drawn across 22 files.",
    "  2. The connectivity tolerance is derived per PLACEMENT INSTANCE instead of",
    "     from the whole drawing's bounding box, so one corrupt coordinate cannot",
    "     set the tolerance for every piece in the file. The small 'lines' /",
    "     'droppedExact' movements on 8 files are the tighter tolerance no longer",
    "     collapsing genuinely distinct nearby geometry into a 'duplicate'.",
    "  PATTERN COUNTS ARE UNCHANGED ON EVERY FILE except SN1252 (28 -> 29): 27 of",
    "  its 28 instances used to fall back to legacy grouping because the inflated",
    "  tolerance made every vertex read as one point; 24 now classify, its one",
    "  corrupt block still yields legacy pieces, and its kept lines drop",
    "  15,620 -> 11,071. ORPHANS STAYED 0 ON EVERY FILE.",
    "",
    "Files with no closed ASTM layer-1 chain at all (3380, 2927) are pinned to",
    "their pre-ADR-0091 legacy count. DM7549 (2/25) and MHB001 (4/45) still have",
    "instances whose layer-1 chains genuinely do not close (a real gap or spur in",
    "the boundary polyline, not a tolerance artefact) and fall back per instance;",
    "their totals equal the INSERT count anyway. A change to any row is a",
    "regression unless a follow-up re-pins it deliberately with the reason recorded.",
    "Excluded on purpose: 2892XL-new.dxf (24 legacy pieces, slow parse - too slow",
    "for CI), the three 16-36 MB size-run files, and 2756.dxf / 2938 (no supported",
    "entities; unchanged 'empty' rejection)."
  ],
